                <pb facs="0951" n="831" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg831"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Eddy to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-11-25"><hi rendition="#italic">November 25,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Eddy reports that about 100 Jews were killed and wounded in Warsaw; that
                    great destitution prevails among the poorer classes, but that Jews have suffered
                    no more than Christians. Bread and provisions to the value of 10,000 rubles are
                    being distributed daily. As far as known no Jews have been killed in the
                    district of Batum. Seven Jews were killed and 25 wounded in the Riga district,
                    and little or no destitution prevails there. Suffering and destitution at Odessa
                    are great; 560 Jews were killed and 2,000 are in the hospitals.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
